User care practices significantly influence core condition at end-of-first-life, affecting remanufacturing feasibility and economics. Products designed without user guidance often experience preventable degradation reducing remanufacturing viability. Clear care guidance enables users to maximize core preservation while maintaining normal product functionality.

Core preservation guidance creates shared responsibility between manufacturers and users for material value retention. User education builds awareness that care practices influence product's future remanufacturing potential. Care guidance documents become valuable assets when products enter remanufacturing cycles.